# Victor, Valgavoth's Seneschal's count of resolutions is per turn: on turn 3 and again on
# turn 5 Bot1 puts one enchantment onto the battlefield, and each is the first resolution of that turn, so each surveils 2
# and neither makes Bot2 discard. Bot2's own Authority of the Consuls entering on turn 2 is not an enchantment Bot1
# controls: it is no resolution. Turn 3: Bot1 draws Hill Giant, sees Lightning Bolt and Counterspell, bins the Bolt and
# keeps Counterspell on top. Turn 5: Bot1 draws Counterspell and sees two Plains, keeping both.

